# OnePlus 9 Pro / LineageOS 24.0 / Android 17 / Linux 5.4.302 QGKI
# Target: current Forgejo SukiSU builtin-new branch HEAD (fetched at build time).
# This patch carries Linux 5.4-only compatibility and device-hook adaptations.
# KPM remains disabled. Apply after the kernel patch; strict --fuzz=0 preflight
# must pass against the fetched upstream HEAD before using this adaptation.
#
# Compared with the previous SukiSU patch:
# - Retain the proven 5.4 SELinux policy snapshot adapter and seccomp-safe manager handling.
# - Keep the SU path, kernel inline-hook, UID observer, SUSFS AVC and FD authorization fixes.
# - Do NOT add a second sdcard monitor start: the base source already starts it once in EVENT_BOOT_COMPLETED.
# - Preserve only KSU-owned SELinux allow-rule snapshots so Zygisk Next rules are not rewound.
# - Limit repeated successful sucompat, already-root, and FD lifecycle messages to once per callsite.

